# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# NVIDIA_API_KEY: Optional NVIDIA NIM API key for fast multi-model vision failover (Nemotron 3.5 Super VL, Nemotron 3 Nano Omni, Step-5, Gemma-4).
NVIDIA_API_KEY="MY_NVIDIA_API_KEY"
# NVIDIA_MODELS: optional comma-separated priority list of NVIDIA NIM vision models.
# NVIDIA_MODELS="nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b,nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning,stepfun-ai/step-5-preview,google/gemma-4-31b-it"

# GEMINI_MODEL: optional, the vision-capable model that verifies every setup from the chart screenshot + OHLC (default gemini-3.1-flash-lite).
# GEMINI_MIN_INTERVAL_MS: optional, spacing between Gemini calls (default 12000 for the free tier). A call that would wait too long becomes AI_UNAVAILABLE.
#
# EXECUTION POLICY (what may trade automatically). Safe defaults are shown:
# AI_UNAVAILABLE_POLICY=block            block | allow_engine_only. With allow_engine_only, a setup is traded on the engine result alone when Gemini is down. It is NEVER called visually verified.
# AI_ALLOW_VALID_WITH_RISK=1             1/0. VALID_WITH_RISK = valid pattern with market-quality warnings (countertrend, mixed indicators...).
# AI_ALLOW_COUNTERTREND=1                1/0. Allow countertrend setups to trade (they are always labelled COUNTERTREND RISK).
# AI_REQUIRE_SCREENSHOT=1                1/0. When 1, a setup only trades after the AI really received and confirmed the chart screenshot.
# MAX_SIGNAL_AGE_SEC=                    optional. Default: the larger of 20 s and half a candle.
# TRADE_PIN: optional. When set, placing trades / AI Trading / account switching needs this PIN (the app asks once).
# NO_BRIDGE=1: do not start the Python bridge from server.ts (only for testing).

# HYBRID AI LAYER (shown as `hybrid` on /api/engines; AutoTrading reads it only through the gate configured below)
# HYBRID_MODEL_PATH=models/hybrid_model.json   trained model written by `python3 ml/train.py`. Without it there is NO probability (null), never an invented one.
# HYBRID_MODE=AUTO                             A | B | C | D | AUTO (D when a usable model is loaded, otherwise B, and the response says so)
# HYBRID_ALLOW_SYNTHETIC_MODEL=0               a model trained on synthetic data is refused unless this is 1 (plumbing tests only)

# HYBRID x AUTOTRADING (src/hybridGate.ts, src/executionGate.ts). Safe defaults shown.
# HYBRID_AUTOTRADE=veto                  off | advisory | veto | require
#                                        off: AutoTrading ignores the hybrid verdict. advisory: the AI sees it and it is logged, nothing is blocked.
#                                        veto (default): the hybrid layer may BLOCK a setup it positively disagrees with (indicator gate / model probability / conflict / opposite side). "No opinion" never blocks.
#                                        require: a trade also needs the hybrid layer to confirm the same side. It can only ever remove trades, never add or loosen one.
# MAX_ENTRY_DEVIATION_ATR=0.35           order is cancelled when the price moved more than this many ATR(14) since the signal candle closed
# MAX_ENTRY_DELAY_SEC=45                 order must be sent within this many seconds after the signal candle closed (AI time included). ASSUMPTION: tune it to your measured AI latency
# MAX_STAKE=                             optional hard cap on the stake of one trade
# HYBRID_LOG_PATH=data/hybrid_log.jsonl  execution log (candidates, gate results, orders, outcomes). Read it at /api/hybrid/log and /api/hybrid/analytics

# CLASSIC / PRO MODE (see docs/MODES.md)
# ALLOW_CUSTOM_EXPIRY=1   1 (default): a time frame / expiry YOU pick in Classic or Pro mode is accepted by the execution gate.
#                         0: strict policy only. Every auto trade must use the 5-minute chart with a 5-minute expiry, or one candle on other charts.
# MAX_STAKE also caps every MTG recovery stake: MTG stops instead of going past it.

# MULTI-AGENT CANDIDATE BROADCAST (docs/CANDIDATE_BROADCAST.md)
# SWEEP_TF=300                           candle size the market agents watch (30 | 60 | 120 | 180 | 300). Default 300 = completed M5 candles.
# CANDIDATE_AI_CONCURRENCY=2             how many candidates may be in the AI / hybrid verification at once (freshest first; stale ones are skipped, not queued forever)
# CANDIDATE_AI_TIMEOUT_MS=60000          an AI / hybrid answer that takes longer than this rejects its candidate (never an approval)
# MAX_ENTRY_DELAY_SEC (above)            also the freshness limit of a candidate: it is not verified or traded later than this after its candle closed

# TELEGRAM LOSS NOTIFICATIONS (optional: sends chart + indicators screenshot and trade reasons on every lost trade)
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN="MY_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID="MY_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID"
